  "visual": {
    "visualType": "textbox",
    "objects": {
      "general": [
        {
          "properties": {
            "paragraphs": [
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "How to read this report",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI Semibold",
                      "fontSize": "18pt",
                      "color": "#1F1F1F"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "horizontalTextAlignment": "left"
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": " ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI",
                      "fontSize": "8pt",
                      "color": "#1F1F1F"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "horizontalTextAlignment": "left"
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "The rule. ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI Semibold",
                      "fontSize": "12pt",
                      "color": "#1F1F1F"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": "To win outright, a presidential candidate needs the most votes nationwide and at least a quarter (25%) of the votes in at least two-thirds of the states. Abuja (the Federal Capital Territory) counts as a state here, so there are 37. The 2023 election courts treated Abuja like a 37th state but did not say whether that means 25 or 24 states. We use 25 (two-thirds of 37, rounded up); 24 (two-thirds of the 36 states) is offered on the simulator. This is our reading of section 134 of the Constitution, checked against an unofficial copy.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI",
                      "fontSize": "12pt",
                      "color": "#1F1F1F"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "horizontalTextAlignment": "left"
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": " ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI",
                      "fontSize": "8pt",
                      "color": "#1F1F1F"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "horizontalTextAlignment": "left"
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "What the numbers are. ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI Semibold",
                      "fontSize": "12pt",
                      "color": "#1F1F1F"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": "The 2023 result in each state, put together from five copies of INEC's declaration, because INEC's own state sheet is not public. PDP and NNPP state totals add up to INEC's national declaration with no adjustment; for APC and Labour they match because three disputed figures were chosen to make them match. The minor candidates' column is 4,858 votes too high nationally, and nobody can yet say where.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI",
                      "fontSize": "12pt",
                      "color": "#1F1F1F"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "horizontalTextAlignment": "left"
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": " ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI",
                      "fontSize": "8pt",
                      "color": "#1F1F1F"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "horizontalTextAlignment": "left"
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "What the simulator assumes. ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI Semibold",
                      "fontSize": "12pt",
                      "color": "#1F1F1F"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": "A change in vote share adds the same number of points in every state of a zone. Turnout changes only the candidate's own 2023 voters. Other candidates gain or lose in proportion to their 2023 votes. The voters are the 2023 voters: nobody who registered since 2023 is included. No new candidates or boundary changes, and no merged parties unless you switch the coalition On. It is a what-if tool, not a forecast: it says nothing about how likely any what-if is.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI",
                      "fontSize": "12pt",
                      "color": "#1F1F1F"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "horizontalTextAlignment": "left"
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": " ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI",
                      "fontSize": "8pt",
                      "color": "#1F1F1F"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "horizontalTextAlignment": "left"
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Merging parties. ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI Semibold",
                      "fontSize": "12pt",
                      "color": "#1F1F1F"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": "Two pages add 2023 votes together. \"Merge two parties\" joins a lead party and a partner; \"Head to head\" sets that coalition against one party or another coalition. You choose how many of the partner's voters follow (an assumption: no published figure exists); those who do not follow stay home. These are 2023 votes recombined, not a forecast. On the What-if simulator, \"Use the coalition\" (Off by default) applies every slider to the coalition instead of the candidate. Only \"NDC (Obi + Kwankwaso)\" is a real ticket.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI",
                      "fontSize": "12pt",
                      "color": "#1F1F1F"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "horizontalTextAlignment": "left"
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": " ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI",
                      "fontSize": "8pt",
                      "color": "#1F1F1F"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "horizontalTextAlignment": "left"
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Words used. ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI Semibold",
                      "fontSize": "12pt",
                      "color": "#1F1F1F"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": "\"Won\" (or \"Secured\") = a quarter of the vote or more in a state; \"Within reach\" = 20% to just under a quarter; \"Out of reach\" = under 20%. \"The deciding state\" = the weakest state the candidate needs to reach 25 (or 24). Exact definitions and formulas are on the Technical notes page.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI",
                      "fontSize": "12pt",
                      "color": "#1F1F1F"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "horizontalTextAlignment": "left"
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": " ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI",
                      "fontSize": "8pt",
                      "color": "#1F1F1F"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "horizontalTextAlignment": "left"
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "What it does not claim. ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI Semibold",
                      "fontSize": "12pt",
                      "color": "#1F1F1F"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": "It is not an electoral authority and not INEC's figures. It has no local-government detail. Small changes near a quarter of the vote are within the data's uncertainty: for example, Bola Tinubu's 29 states in 2023 include Adamawa, where he was only 96 votes above a quarter.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI",
                      "fontSize": "12pt",
                      "color": "#1F1F1F"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "horizontalTextAlignment": "left"
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": " ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI",
                      "fontSize": "8pt",
                      "color": "#1F1F1F"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "horizontalTextAlignment": "left"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
